<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

  <!--
    A Dog Said... Animal Prosthetics 2 (packageId SamBucher.ADogSaidAnimalProsthetics2, Workshop 3238353862)
    lets an animal receive prostheses by listing it in one of three abstract recipe categories:

      ADS_Cat1  basic replacements, the small critters
      ADS_Cat2  Cat1 and simple prosthetic limbs, non-trainable and non-packable animals
      ADS_Cat3  Cat2 and bionics, trainable and packable animals, and cats

    Each category lists the animals that may use its recipes, and the three lists nest, so an animal of
    category 3 is written into all three. The teshi is trainable to intermediate and as large as a bear,
    and the bears, wolves, wargs and cougars are category 3 there, so it goes in all three.

    The patch is conditional on the category existing in the merged defs, not on a mod name: with the
    other mod absent it finds nothing and does nothing, and no log line is written. ADS2 asks any mod
    that builds this in to load BEFORE it, which About.xml declares in loadBefore. It is an optional
    integration: About.xml declares no modDependencies and there is no LoadFolders.
  -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/RecipeDef[@Name="ADS_Cat3"]/recipeUsers</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>/Defs/RecipeDef[
        @Name="ADS_Cat3" or
        @Name="ADS_Cat2" or
        @Name="ADS_Cat1"
      ]/recipeUsers</xpath>
      <value>
        <li>Teshi</li>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
